---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO, SITE_REPO } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How the Moss website and the Moss software handle your data.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <div class="prose">
      <span class="kicker">Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Short version: this website collects nothing, and the Moss software keeps your data on your own machine.</p>
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts, no cookies, no analytics, no advertising and no trackers.</li>
        <li>The only thing stored in your browser is your light or dark theme choice, in local storage, and it never leaves your device.</li>
        <li>The site is static and hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may keep standard server logs; see <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>The Moss software</h2>
      <p>Moss runs on a machine you control. Server files, worlds, console logs and backups stay there.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Sign-in.</b> Moss uses a Supabase project that you create. Moss stores each user's account ID, email address and role in its local database, and verifies sign-in tokens locally. Passwords are handled by Supabase and are never seen by Moss.</li>
        <li><b>Activity log.</b> Moss records who did what (starting a server, editing a file) so the owner can review it. It stays in your instance.</li>
        <li><b>Downloads.</b> When you ask for a server jar, Java runtime or plugin, Moss contacts Mojang, PaperMC, Purpur, Fabric, Modrinth or Adoptium. Moss sends no telemetry to its authors.</li>
        <li><b>OAuth sign-in.</b> If you enable GitHub or Google sign-in, Moss only requests basic profile and email scopes to identify the account. It never requests access to repositories, mail, files or contacts.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>Remove a user in Moss to revoke their access, and delete their Supabase account to remove the sign-in itself. Delete the Moss data directory to remove everything Moss stored.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or concerns: open an issue on <a href={SITE_REPO} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. Security reports go through <a href={`${REPO}/security/advisories/new`} rel="noopener">private vulnerability reporting</a>.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--faint);font-size:14px">Last updated October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
